// expect-exit: 0
//
// `Instant`'s four operations, and its two refusals (cycle 0.2.0; TM-215,
// TM-216; `TIME_MODEL.md` M-2 and M-4, `HOST.md` H-6). (Since cycle 0.2.4b
// there is a third, `instant_since`'s of a difference past `Duration`'s
// range, which `tests/unit/instant_since_edges.npk` holds -- TM-242.)
//
// ASKS: two readings of one clock, built by `instant_of` -- does
// `instant_since` give their distance, does `instant_add` of that distance to
// the earlier give back the later, does `instant_cmp` call them `Equal`, does
// `instant_add` keep the clock it was given, a `Boottime` reading's as well as
// a `Monotonic` one's, does a `Vec<Instant>` hand a reading of each clock
// back, and are a `Boottime` reading and a `Monotonic` one refused by both
// `instant_since` and `instant_cmp`?
//
// MATTERS BECAUSE a reading of one clock less a reading of the other is a
// number that means nothing (H-6: `Boottime` counts suspend, `Monotonic` does
// not), and the refusal is the only thing between a caller and that number.
// Every `Result` is read through `is_error` first, and `value` only after.
//
// EXIT CODES, clear of every arm code (TM-152): 10 `instant_since` refused a
// same-clock pair; 11 its distance is not 3 500 ns; 12 `instant_cmp` refused a
// same-clock pair; 13 the sum is not `Equal` to the later reading; 14
// `instant_add` did not keep the clock it was given; 15 a `Vec<Instant>` did
// not hand a reading back (both types derive `Copy`, TM-215, and
// `Vec<T: Copy>` asks it since cycle 0.2.0b); 16 `instant_since` accepted two
// clocks; 17 `instant_cmp` accepted two clocks. EACH WAS SEEN RED ON A MUTANT
// AT CYCLE 0.2.1'S PLANNING, on both legs, in a copy of the tree
// (`meta/roadmap/done/0.2/0.2.1.md`, step 1): 10 and 12 `instant_since`'s and
// `instant_cmp`'s clock tests inverted; 11 `instant_since`'s operands swapped;
// 13 `instant_add` subtracting; 14 `instant_add`'s clock hard-coded, to
// `Boottime` (the first of its two lines) and to `Monotonic` (the second); 15
// the `Boottime` element's read replaced by a vacant reading, and by one that
// keeps its nanoseconds and loses its clock; 16 and 17 the two cross-clock
// tests deleted.
//
// A CLOCK IS CHECKED THROUGH A `Boottime` READING, AND THAT IS THE POINT.
// `Monotonic` is `InstantClock`'s first variant, tag 0 -- the value a vacant
// read or a hard-coded default produces -- so a check that a clock is
// `Monotonic` passes both (the workbench `PLAYBOOK.md` §9: a positive test
// whose expected value is the vacant value tests nothing). Until cycle 0.2.1
// exit 14 read the clock of a `Monotonic` reading alone, and an `instant_add`
// that hard-coded `Monotonic` passed it at exit 0 on both legs, as 0.2.0's
// verifier measured; exit 15 read the clock of a `Monotonic` element alone;
// and this header said each exit "was seen red on its mutant at planning",
// which 10, 12 and 14 never were.
//
// THE `failsafe` NAMES WHAT `NITPICK-REACH-002` ASKS of a root importing
// `span` and `core/vec`: `span`'s eleven (`cal.ETimeValue`, the floor and
// `cal`'s four arithmetic arms, `SAFETY.md` S-4) and `LimitViolated`, which
// `Vec`'s `ListLen` adds -- twelve.
mod:instant_ops;

use "../../src/span/span.npk".*;
use "../../src/core/vec.npk".*;

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
    Instant:a = raw instant_of(1000i64, InstantClock.Monotonic);
    Instant:b = raw instant_of(4500i64, InstantClock.Monotonic);
    Instant:x = raw instant_of(4500i64, InstantClock.Boottime);
    Result<Duration>:d = instant_since(b, a);
    if (d.is_error) { exit 10i32; }
    if (d.value.ns != 3500i64) { exit 11i32; }
    Instant:c = raw instant_add(a, d.value);
    Instant:y = raw instant_add(x, d.value);
    if (c.clock != InstantClock.Monotonic) { exit 14i32; }
    if (y.clock != InstantClock.Boottime) { exit 14i32; }
    Result<Ordering>:o = instant_cmp(c, b);
    if (o.is_error) { exit 12i32; }
    if (o.value != Ordering.Equal) { exit 13i32; }
    Vec<Instant>:v = raw vec_init::<Instant>(2i64);
    drop vec_push(@v, b);
    drop vec_push(@v, x);
    Instant:r1 = raw vec_at(v, 0i64);
    Instant:r2 = raw vec_at(v, 0i64);
    Instant:r3 = raw vec_at(v, 1i64);
    drop vec_free(@v);
    if (r1.ns != 4500i64 || r2.ns != 4500i64 || r2.clock != InstantClock.Monotonic) { exit 15i32; }
    if (r3.ns != 4500i64 || r3.clock != InstantClock.Boottime) { exit 15i32; }
    Result<Duration>:e = instant_since(x, a);
    if (!(e.is_error)) { exit 16i32; }
    Result<Ordering>:f = instant_cmp(x, a);
    if (!(f.is_error)) { exit 17i32; }
    exit 0i32;
};

func:failsafe = int32(Error:e) {
    pick (e) {
        (cal.ETimeValue)    { exit 80i32; },
        (HeapBadRequest)    { exit 91i32; },
        (HeapOom)           { exit 92i32; },
        (IntOverflow)       { exit 93i32; },
        (OutOfBounds)       { exit 94i32; },
        (Unreachable)       { exit 95i32; },
        (WildLeak)          { exit 96i32; },
        (DivByZero)         { exit 97i32; },
        (DivOverflow)       { exit 98i32; },
        (LimitViolated)     { exit 109i32; },
        (StackExhausted)    { exit 106i32; },
        (MachineFault)      { exit 107i32; },
        (*)                 { exit 99i32; }
    }
    exit 9i32;
};
